							<tr>
								<td><font face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><a class="NV3" href="addnews.asp">Submit Your News!</font></a></b></font><br><br>
								
								<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4796" target="_new"><B>Fallout Tactics Designer Diary VI</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">Fallout Tactics Designer Diary
As the game continues to progress towards its projected spring release, Senior Designer  Chris Taylor of Interplay offers a look into the critical area of game balance for both single- and multiplayer modes in his new Fallout Tactics Designer Diary, Part VI.</font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4795" target="_new"><B>Carnivores: Ice Age Review</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">Fans of the previous Carnivores games will be immediately at home in what looks to be the last of the series (developer Action Forms Ltd is moving on to Duke Nukem: Endangered Species). And an appropriate end to the series it is, bringing armchair hunters face-to-snout with the ancestors of the tigers, bears, birds, wolves and elephants long available in hunting titles set on present-day Earth. </font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4794" target="_new"><B>Combat Command 2: Danger Forward Review</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">Shrapnel Games has just released a sequel to its World War II wargame Combat Command. Developers Boku will be well-known to fans of other Shrapnel-published games such as Horse and Musket. In Combat Command 2: Danger Forward, they've managed to produce a solid, no-frills game, yet one with modest system requirements and something of a novel twist in its emphasis on airborne and amphibious operations. 

</font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4793" target="_new"><B>The Corporate Machine Review</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">The Corporate Machine isn't an accurate business simulator. It's a strategy game with a good many business elements, but these are abstracted for gameplay purposes. If you want to count beans, you're in the wrong place. If you want an innovative, challenging game that can run on a low spec PC, read on. 

</font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4792" target="_new"><B>Baldur's Gate 2 expansion announced</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">Black Isle Studios, the role-playing game division of Interplay Entertainment Corp. (Nasdaq: IPLY - news), and BioWare Corp. announced today plans to develop an expansion product to the award-winning role-playing game Baldur's Gate(TM) II: Shadows of Amn(TM). Entitled Baldur's Gate(TM) II: Throne of Bhaal(TM), the add-on product expands and enriches the gameplay experience by adding several new locations, high-level spells and powerful new characters to the Baldur's Gate game. Set in the Forgotten Realms® campaign world of the Dungeons & Dragons game, Throne of Bhaal is the ultimate conclusion of the Baldur's Gate legend as gamers fulfill their destiny as the child of Bhaal</font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="2"><P><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4791" target="_new"><B>More Mafia news</B></a> <small>(3/2)</small></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1">Mafia tells the story of a young cab driver named Tommy whose life takes a major turn the day a couple of gangsters order him to drive--and drive fast. In the end, they give him a choice: he could either join the family or he could die. Given his options, Tommy chooses to become a gangster himself, starting out in the entry level position of a lowly errand boy.

</font><br></font></small><BR><P><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4790" target="_new"><B>Interview with Mafia developer Daniel Vavra</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4789" target="_new"><B>Dungeon Siege interview</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4788" target="_new"><B>Star Trek Voyager: Elite Force Gets an Add-On Pack</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4787" target="_new"><B>Links expansion announced</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4786" target="_new"><B>Quick Look: The Moon Project</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4785" target="_new"><B>Project IGI: I'm Going In Review</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4784" target="_new"><B>Dave Mirra Freestyle BMX Review</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4783" target="_new"><B>Ducati World Racing Challenge Review</B></a></font><BR><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"><a class="NV3" HREF="redirect.asp?WWID=4782" target="_new"><B>Harley-Davidson: Wheels of Freedom Review</B></a></font><BR><p align="right"><a href="http://www.wewp.com/wewpwire" class="nv3"><font face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">More Wewp!Wire News &gt;&gt;</font></a></td>
